%% Fast-Session Commit + Notification Event Hand-off Sequence
%% Descriptive. Specializes system 05-runtime/fast-session; ADR-005.
%% NOTE: no outbox/broker/queue mechanism is implied. Emitting module owns the atomic hand-off.

sequenceDiagram
    participant Teacher
    participant Web as Web / API process
    participant EO as Educational Operations (emitting module)
    participant Store as Persistence (Open)
    participant Worker as Worker process
    participant Push as Push Delivery interface

    Teacher->>Web: open group session
    Web->>EO: Session Instance Planned to Open

    loop per student
        Teacher->>Web: tap Present/Absent (or Studied/Not-Studied/Skip)
        Web->>EO: authn/authz + context - validate transition / invariants
        alt Present or Studied
            EO->>Store: persist record (tenant-scoped)
        else Absent or Not-Studied
            EO->>Store: ATOMIC commit - record + durable notification event hand-off (within emitting module boundary)
        else Skip
            EO->>EO: advance - no record, no event
        end
        Web-->>Teacher: return - UI advances (no wait on delivery)
    end

    Teacher->>Web: close session
    Web->>EO: Session Instance Open to Closed

    Note over Worker: internal worker job (not a client-facing operation)
    Worker->>Store: consume durable event hand-off
    Worker->>Push: dispatch (async - may fail independently)

    Note over Teacher,Push: Correction - Closed to Reopened to flip to Closed. Prior notifications stand - a new Absent/Not-Studied may fire a new hand-off.
